ok - reclaim: a herdr rebind is created in the session the record names, never the ambient one
ok - reclaim: a herdr reclaim rebinds the endpoint and leaves the whole rest of the task alone
ok - reclaim: a rebind refused from a plain shell reports the real cause, not a fabricated session mismatch
ok - reclaim: a re-created herdr endpoint gets its own workspace after its owner's child block
ok - reclaim: a second mate's re-created worker lands in that second mate's child block
ok - reclaim: an earlier projection that is gone is retired and the endpoint is projected again
ok - reclaim: a re-created herdr endpoint stays flat when presentation is off, below the floor, contended, or still has an earlier projection
ok - reclaim: a failed ordering move leaves the re-created workspace in Herdr's current order, like a fresh spawn
